    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41969" root="وشر" body-key="w">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَشَرَ</span></b> , (S, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَشْرٌ</span>, (TA,) <i>He sawed</i> a
piece of wood with a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِيشَار</span>; a dial. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشَر</span>;
(S, K;) <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَشَرَ</span>. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وشَرَتْ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَشِرُ</span>, (Msb,)
inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَشْرٌ</span>, (S, K,) <i>She</i> (a woman) <i>sharpened</i> (S,
Msb, K) her teeth, (S, K,) or her canine teeth,
(Msb.) <i>and made</i> them <i>thin</i> [<i>and serrated</i>], (S,
Msb, K,) meaning their edges: (TA:) [as also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشَرَتْ</span>.] See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَاشِرَةٌ</span>.

